{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"openSUSE-SU-2026:22272-1","published":"2026-11-12T07:01:46Z","modified":"2026-11-14T17:23:13.372169541Z","related":["CVE-2026-103658","CVE-2026-75818","CVE-2026-75819","CVE-2026-75820"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-103658","CVE-2026-75818","CVE-2026-75819","CVE-2026-75820"],"summary":"Security update for aspell","details":"This update for aspell fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-75818: heap-based buffer overflow in the decompressor in `prog/prezip.c` can lead to memory corruption and\n  process crash (bsc#1284337).\n- CVE-2026-75819: out-of-bounds read in `ReadOnlyDict::load()` of `readonly_ws.cpp` can lead to heap memory disclosure\n  or application crash (bsc#1284338).\n- CVE-2026-75820: integer truncation in `WritableDict::add() ` of ` modules/speller/default/writable.cpp` can lead to\n  heap corruption (bsc#1284339).\n- CVE-2026-103658: Arbitrary code execution via crafted dictionary file (bsc#1285066).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"aspell","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/aspell&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"aspell":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1","aspell-devel":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1","aspell-ispell":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1","aspell-spell":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1","libaspell15":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1","libpspell15":"0.60.8.1-160000.3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/openSUSE-SU-2026:22272-1.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1284337"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1284338"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1284339"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1285066"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-103658"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-75818"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https:/